Trion Net Send History document

v1.00 - First public release , wich worked fine on my system

v1.01 - Problems, problems, problems on v1.00, but i could not find the
        cause... I tried out several options where the bug could be, but
        nothing... Until i chat with Pascal Dreissen, and we discovered
        the problem... TNS searches for a point number in the node numbers,
        and when somebody didn't use it, it hanged like hell!
        This problem is solved, so you can fill in your node numbers without
        a point now... Also Pascal mentioned the origin, wich was a great
        commercial for my BBS (gna gna), but okay, it's not nice to do such
        things, so i added a little code that reads the origin.list and
        picks random a origin (if you have more than one)...